====================================================================
ASSIGNMENT 1
Write a program that displays the Net Salary (SAL + COMM) of an
employee entered at run time from EMP table.
(Use NVL Function)
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> ACCEPT P_EMPNO PROMPT 'Enter Employee Number : '

sql> SELECT EMPNO,
            ENAME,
            SAL,
            COMM,
            SAL + NVL(COMM,0) AS NETSAL
     FROM EMP
     WHERE EMPNO='&P_EMPNO';

Sample Input:
-------------

Enter Employee Number : 7499

Output:
-------

EMPNO   ENAME   SAL    COMM   NETSAL
------  ------  -----  -----  ------
7499    ALLEN   1600    300    1900


Another Example:
----------------

Enter Employee Number : 7369

Output:
-------

EMPNO   ENAME   SAL    COMM   NETSAL
------  ------  -----  -----  ------
7369    SMITH    800    NULL    800

====================================================================

Explanation:
------------
NVL(COMM,0) replaces NULL commission values with 0.

Formula:
NETSAL = SAL + NVL(COMM,0)

If COMM is NULL, Oracle treats it as 0 while calculating NETSAL.
